In this short podcast episode (Short #313), Bryan talks about why you're not done with a furnace service call or installation just because it lit. It lit. That doesn't mean you're done. Ignition is just one part of the furnace sequence of operations, and the furnace still needs to deliver heat and vent flue gases safely.&#13;
&#13;
 The key takeaway here is that if we only focus on making sure "it lit," we could miss overfiring, poor air delivery, intermittent limit problems, or venting…

