In this short podcast episode, Bryan covers why and how to test heat pump defrost during maintenance. Heat pumps need defrost because the outdoor coil absorbs heat in heating mode. Moisture collects and freezes on the coil during this process, and the rate at which it happens depends on the temperature and the amount of moisture in the outdoor air. Frost interferes with heat transfer and airflow and must be defrosted; the reversing valve shifts and auxiliary heat turns on.&#13;
